## Quick Answer

A whole house renovation has no single price because "whole house" covers everything from paint and floors to a gut down to the studs. National 2026 cost guides put a **cosmetic whole-house update at about $15 to $60 per sq ft** and a **gut renovation at about $60 to $150 per sq ft**. Around Seattle and the Eastside, where labor and code requirements cost more, a Seattle architecture firm gives a planning range of **$300 to $550 per sq ft** for full high-end remodels.

The fastest way to a real number is to price the house room by room. Seattle's 2025 costs for the big items: **$95,542** for a midrange major kitchen, **$36,146** for a midrange bathroom, **$29,743** for fiber-cement siding and **$24,029** for vinyl windows (Cost vs Value 2025).

## Three Levels of "Whole House"

| Level | What it includes | Planning range |
|---|---|---|
| Cosmetic refresh | Paint, flooring, fixtures, lighting, hardware; layout and systems stay | About $15-$60 per sq ft (national) |
| Major renovation | New kitchen and baths, some walls moved, electrical and plumbing updates, windows | Build it room by room from the table below |
| Gut renovation | Interior taken to the studs, new systems, insulation, layout changes | About $60-$150 per sq ft (national); $300-$550 per sq ft for high-end Seattle and Eastside projects |

National figures come from [HomeGuide](https://homeguide.com/costs/house-remodeling-cost) and [Angi](https://www.angi.com/articles/complete-house-renovation-cost.htm) 2026 guides. The high-end Seattle range is a planning figure published by [Piper Cole Architects](https://pipercolearchitects.net/million-dollar-remodel-seattle-eastside/) in October 2026. The spread between them is real: a national average includes small, simple houses and modest finishes, while a Seattle gut renovation includes engineering, energy code upgrades and higher labor rates.

## Seattle 2025 Costs by Project

The [2025 Cost vs Value report](https://www.jlconline.com/cost-vs-value/2025/pacific/seattle-wa/) prices common projects for the Seattle market. Use it to build your budget item by item:

| Project | Seattle job cost | Recouped at resale |
|---|---|---|
| Minor kitchen remodel, midrange | $32,271 | 118.1% |
| Major kitchen remodel, midrange | $95,542 | 53.1% |
| Major kitchen remodel, upscale | $188,401 | 38.7% |
| Bathroom remodel, midrange | $36,146 | 46.8% |
| Bathroom remodel, upscale | $107,451 | 35.3% |
| Universal design bathroom | $58,151 | 59.2% |
| Basement remodel | $68,358 | 68.0% |
| Siding replacement, fiber-cement | $29,743 | 56.7% |
| Window replacement, vinyl | $24,029 | 46.1% |
| Window replacement, wood | $29,669 | 48.4% |
| Entry door replacement, steel | $2,694 | 157.0% |
| Deck addition, composite | $28,639 | 79.6% |

### Example: Building a Budget

Take a two-bathroom house getting a midrange major kitchen, both baths redone midrange, new vinyl windows and new floors through the main level:

- Kitchen: $95,542
- Two bathrooms: 2 x $36,146 = $72,292
- Windows: $24,029
- Flooring, 1,000 sq ft of luxury vinyl plank at $4-$16 per sq ft installed: $4,000-$16,000

That adds up to roughly **$196,000 to $208,000** before paint, electrical upgrades, any wall changes and a 10-15% contingency. This is why most whole house projects in the area land well above the national per-square-foot averages.

## What Drives the Cost Up

- **Moving walls.** Removing a load-bearing wall runs roughly $1,200-$10,000 in national guides, more on multi-story houses. See our [main floor remodel guide](/blog/main-floor-remodel-cost-seattle).
- **Systems.** Moving plumbing, adding circuits, a new electrical panel or HVAC changes.
- **Energy code.** Washington's energy code requires insulating every wall, ceiling and floor cavity you open: at least R-15 in 2x4 walls and R-21 in 2x6 walls ([WAC 51-11R-50300](https://app.leg.wa.gov/wac/default.aspx?cite=51-11R-50300)). Replacement windows must meet the code's U-factor.
- **Substantial alteration.** In Seattle, replacing walls in more than 60% of a house is likely treated as a substantial alteration, which can trigger code upgrades for the whole house ([SDCI Tip 316](https://www.seattle.gov/dpd/publications/cam/cam316.pdf)).
- **Age of the house.** About 45% of homes in King County were built before 1980 (2024 King County Comprehensive Plan). Older homes need an asbestos survey before renovation, and pre-1978 homes need lead-safe work practices.
- **Finish level.** Cabinets, counters, tile and fixtures can double a kitchen or bath between midrange and upscale, as the table shows.

## Permits for a Whole House Renovation

A whole house renovation always needs permits. What changes is the path:

- **Seattle:** interior alterations of a house usually go through a [Subject-to-Field-Inspection permit](https://www.seattle.gov/sdci/permits/permits-we-issue-(a-z)/construction-permit---subject-to-field-inspection), screened in a few days. Larger beams and structural work need stamped plans. Plumbing permits are issued by Public Health, Seattle & King County.
- **Bellevue:** a [single-family remodel permit](https://bellevuewa.gov/city-government/departments/development/permits/residential-building-permits/single-family-remodel-permit) with plan review covers structural changes and includes electrical, mechanical and plumbing. Its median review was 13 days over the 12 months to October 2026; additions took a median of 75 days ([Bellevue data](https://bellevuewaprod.blob.core.windows.net/documentcenter/DSRecords/processing-day-by-permit-type.pdf)).
- **Kirkland:** a permit is needed for interior remodels, for adding, removing or relocating any wall, and for drywall removal ([Kirkland](https://www.kirklandwa.gov/Government/Departments/Development-Services-Center/Do-you-need-a-permit)).
- **Redmond:** a permit is needed for alterations and remodels of an existing home ([Redmond](https://www.redmond.gov/469/Residential-Permits)).

### Asbestos and Lead

The [Puget Sound Clean Air Agency](https://pscleanair.gov/192/Homeowner-Renovation) requires an asbestos survey before renovation; an owner who lives in the house may survey it themselves for a remodel, otherwise an AHERA-certified inspector does it. Under [RCW 49.26](https://app.leg.wa.gov/rcw/default.aspx?cite=49.26&full=true) a contractor may not start until it has a copy of the written survey report. In homes built before 1978, paid work that disturbs paint must follow the EPA's [lead-safe RRP rule](https://www.epa.gov/lead/renovation-repair-and-painting-program).

## How Long It Takes

National surveys show planning takes longer than building. In the [2026 Houzz & Home study](https://st.hzcdn.com/static/econ/2026_U.S._Houzz_and_Home_Study_RenovationTrends.pdf) of 2025 projects, a kitchen remodel took a median of 9.5 months to plan and 5.8 months to build; a primary bathroom 8.4 and 4.8 months. Angi's guide puts major renovations with floor plan or structural changes at 12-15 months overall.

A whole house renovation usually runs in this order:

1. Assessment, scope and budget, asbestos survey
2. Design, engineering for any structural changes, energy code compliance
3. Permits
4. Demolition and rough-in: framing, plumbing, electrical, HVAC, insulation
5. Inspections, drywall, finishes, final inspection

Phasing is possible: many owners do the kitchen and main floor first and the bathrooms and exterior later, which spreads the cost but repeats some setup work.

## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does it cost to renovate a whole house in Seattle?

For a cosmetic refresh, national guides show $15-$60 per sq ft. A full renovation with a new kitchen, baths and windows is better priced room by room: in Seattle's 2025 costs, a midrange kitchen, two midrange baths and new windows alone come to about $192,000. High-end gut renovations around Seattle and the Eastside are planned at $300-$550 per sq ft.

### Is it cheaper to renovate or rebuild?

It depends on the structure. If the foundation, framing and roof are sound, a renovation keeps the most expensive parts of the house. When most walls, systems and the envelope must be replaced, a renovation can trigger the same code upgrades as new construction, and the comparison needs a site-specific estimate.

### Which renovations pay back the most at resale in Seattle?

In the 2025 Cost vs Value data for Seattle, a steel entry door (157%) and a same-layout minor kitchen remodel (118%) recouped more than they cost. Major kitchen and bathroom remodels recouped 35-59%.

### Can I live in the house during a whole house renovation?

Often for part of it. Kitchen and bathroom phases, asbestos abatement and floor refinishing usually mean moving out for a period; phasing the work room by room makes staying possible longer.

